//! flags: -p ssa -b llvm

// Golden-diffs the LLVM the loop from a `map` compiles to through the SSA
// pipeline. `map` lowers to a parfor -- its iterations are independent by
// definition -- and one no schedule has placed on any hardware is emitted as
// the ordinary counted loop it is.
//
// What the golden should show is an ordinary counted loop -- a phi for the
// index, a compare, a back edge -- and nothing left of the block structure
// the conversion went through.
func doubled(a : array[i32, 4]) = map(|x : i32| x * 2, a);

// A loop whose trip count is not known here, so that it cannot simply be
// unrolled away and the loop itself has to come out right.
func scale(n : u32, a : array[f32, n], k : f32) = map(|x : f32| x * k, a);
